      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MASTRETTA (8) ran on from last for third when resuming, and in 2 starts since then, she has set the pace, weakening late for third at her penultimate start, then making all the running 3 weeks ago, all on this track. She gets another crack at the open-grade, and with 4.5kg less to carry, she is set to repeat the dose. SH'BOURNE MIDNIGHT (5) was put aside after a couple of mixed efforts in the winter, and resumes over his pet trip here. A recent trial will have him ready to run a bold race fresh. Follow any market confidence. DISTRUSTFUL AWARD (1) went close to winning a race last prep, and he resumes from a spell without any public trials. He usually gets back in the running, so look for him late, and don't risk him in any wider combos. FAST THINKER (3) is a durable veteran fresh up, and he normally takes a run to hit his straps. He has had 2 trials already this season and is not badly off at the weights for a 14-race winner. Keep safe. EARENDEL (7) is another with top 4 claims.",
